{"reference":"Amos 5","book":"Amos","chapter":5,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"chapter_overview","title":"Overview","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter joins its calls to seek God and establish justice with a severe exposure of public wrongdoing. The poor are trampled, grain is taken from them, and the needy are denied their rights at the gate—the public place where cases are heard. Against that setting, the rejection of feasts, offerings, songs, and music in verses 21–24 is not a rejection of worship as such; it condemns worship practiced alongside exploitation. The image of justice flowing like waters calls for a communal pattern of accountable practice, not a detached slogan.","verse_refs":["Amos 5:18-27","Amos 5:25-27","Amos 5:7-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_amos_005_92522b88df9cc3c685918e76"],"confidence":"medium","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Questions Readers May Have","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"The people who desire the day of YHWH are warned that it will be darkness, danger, and no escape for them. Amos does not provide an end-times timetable here. Zephaniah 1 uses similarly severe imagery for the great Day of YHWH—darkness, distress, battle cry, ruined defenses, and wealth unable to rescue—helping clarify the force of Amos’s reversal of hopeful expectation.","verse_refs":["Amos 5:18-20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_amos_005_f3d878f3ad4c1d2596c440c1"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"},{"id":"block_3","text":"Verses 25–27 raise difficult textual questions. The names rendered Sikkuth and Kiyyun are uncertain divine or cultic designations, so confident identifications with later names or modern groups go beyond what can be established. Acts 7:42–43 quotes a Greek form of this passage with forms rendered Moloch and Rephan. These should be read as part of Greek textual and reception history, rather than casually equated with the names in Amos’s Hebrew form or used against Jewish worship.","verse_refs":["Amos 5:25-27","Amos 5:7-17","Amos 5:7-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_amos_005_7b716618d3f958a23a1f469a"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}